      "writtenOn": "2026-05-11T09:25:02Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "Technically, Francisco already did the work to flag all the files (outside of dawn/node here), so what\u0027s left is already passing the `-Wunsafe-buffer-usage` error. So, it means we are only forcing new files to pass in the future, which is great.\n\nFor `dawn/node`, I will let Dawn owner to decide. It indeed doesn\u0027t impact chrome. This is only a nice to have.\n\n---\n\nIn Chrome, we enabled -WUnsafe-buffer-usage for all code, including tests.\n\nThe rational was:\n- Getting crash instead of undefined behavior in tests is easier to debug.\n- Code in test files is just as likely as any other code to be used as inspiration or even directly copy-n-pasted into production code somewhere. So it is better if we have the same errors surfaced everywhere.",
